{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026011-weapons-equipment-bonuses-and-magic","id":1026011,"title":"Weapons, Equipment Bonuses, and Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-03T10:20:17-08:00","id":1026011,"title":"Weapons, Equipment Bonuses, and Magic","content":"As ever, I'm super sorry if this has come up elsewhere. My search did not yield results.<br /> <br /> One of my players asked today how Fate's &quot;Monkey Paw&quot; (3 dot spell) would affect weapons. The spell reads (just a snippet, but the part that matters): <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The object\u2019s equipment bonus is increased or decreased by the spell\u2019s Potency, which may cause it to become a dice penalty if moved below zero. </div> </div> </div>The question was basically: Does it give a +bonus when you roll to attack, or does it give a bonus to the weapon's damage? This brings up the question, really, of how equipment bonuses and weapons interact. There doesn't appear to be any rules for this in CofD or in M:tAw 2E. Generally, equipment and weapons are kept totally separate in the book, and equipment bonus is always a dice bonus added to the roll to use the equipment (obviously using a knife as equipment makes it equipment for that purpose).<br /> <br /> I know ST fiat could be used here, and the storyteller could say your lucky knife manages to always find it's target (+dice on attack roll) or that it manages to always hit somewhere good when it does (+damage), but I wanted the opinion of everyone else.<br /> <br /> For the sake of consistency and comparison, I looked into Matter, and I found Shaping (2 dot spell), which reads:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> +1 Reach: The mage can alter the shape of solid substances as well. If used to warp a tool or weapon, each point of Potency reduces the subject\u2019s equipment bonus or damage by \u20131. </div> </div> </div>Here, it very specifically states equipment bonus or damage. If that's the case, then I'd read Monkey Paw as not working on weapons at all. Is that the case? Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12020-skewskewskew","name":"skewskewskew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:23:01-08:00","id":1026016,"title":"","content":"I remember this being asked as far as the Open Dev, and I don't remember the answer. Or if it even was answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:28:13-08:00","id":1026020,"title":"","content":"I was once told equipment bonuses do not apply to weapons like that. Specifically when dealing with stakes.<br /> <br /> It was not by a developer but I haven't seen much to make me think otherwise. Unfortunate, but it does sort of make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:49:47-08:00","id":1026042,"title":"","content":"I agree with your interpretation. The Chronicles of Darkness rulebook seems fairly clear that Equipment bonuses apply to dice modifiers, not a weapon's damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:16:09-08:00","id":1026531,"title":"","content":"Given that there are reasons to go either way, why not let the intent of the Mage decide when casting the spell? Or even divide Potency between the two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:14:16-08:00","id":1026620,"title":"","content":"Ability to modify Weapon Rating directly is not equal to applying dice modifiers to the roll. Again, 1DR is little better than +3 dice. 3 Potency per DR sounds like a good rule of thumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:27:44-08:00","id":1026626,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the reason &quot;weapons&quot; and &quot;equipment&quot; are stated separately is because they serve different functions. A crowbar can be used as a tool, granting an equipment bonus to rolls to pry open doors, or it can be used as a weapon, penalizing the wielder's Initiative and dealing its damage rating to whoever they smack with it. Monkey's paw would add to (or subtract from) the former use of a crowbar, but not the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:33:07-08:00","id":1026629,"title":"","content":"I would think Matter would have spells related to weapon damage. I'm personally wondering if it'll be alongside the perfected metals, so waiting for the next book to come out before making any final judgements. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the lack of weapon damage is deliberate, forcing a focus on casting spells in combat instead of buff-and-attacking. Mages are defined by their spell casting, after all, so it might be a deliberate thematic call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:36:14-08:00","id":1026633,"title":"","content":"At two dots, Forces' Kinetic Blow lets you add Weapon Rating to unarmed attacks and, with a Reach, weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:40:01-08:00","id":1026634,"title":"","content":"Wow. I forgot how ridiculous is Kinetic Blow.<br /> Then I remembered what else you can do at 2 dots and it wasn't as ridiculous as I thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T21:01:10-08:00","id":1026843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026011-weapons-equipment-bonuses-and-magic?p=1026531#post1026531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that there are reasons to go either way, why not let the intent of the Mage decide when casting the spell? Or even divide Potency between the two?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't include in my original, but this is for a MUX, which is a &quot;big&quot; online continually operating game. Many scenes happen without a designated storyteller, and the results can be chaotic at time, so we try to clarify rules whenever possible.<br /> <br /> Thanks everyone else!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12020-skewskewskew","name":"skewskewskew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}